只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"本地优先的文献知识库 RAG(DeepSeek Harness 插件):混合检索正文与图注,把模糊记忆定位到具体段落与图表,DOI 一键直达原文。Local-first literature RAG for DSH — turn a fuzzy memory into an exact passage/figure, one-click DOI to source.","id":"gh:1335816329","install_available":true,"language":"Python","name":"dsh-kb-rag","slug":"Breeze136/dsh-kb-rag","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","knowledge-base","literature","rag","zotero"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"本地优先的文献知识库 RAG(DeepSeek Harness 插件):混合检索正文与图注,把模糊记忆定位到具体段落与图表,DOI 一键直达原文。Local-first literature RAG "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"for DSH — turn a fuzzy memory into an exact passage/figure, one-click DOI to source."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# kb-rag: local literature RAG with passage-level provenance"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | Chinese"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"kb-rag is a local literature knowledge base for DSH (DeepSeek Harness) and other MCP clients. It ind"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"exes PDFs and Zotero libraries into one SQLite file, then returns the passages that answer a questio"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"n. Each result carries its section, physical page and DOI, and the citations attached to that passag"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"e, including whether the cited work is already in your library."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Indexing, embedding and reranking run on your machine. There is no API cost and nothing is uploaded."},{"id":"p5s2","text":" Warm queries take 0.33-0.38 s in `quick` mode and 1.4-1.9 s in `deep`; the first call after a resta"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"rt can take up to 8.9 s while the models load."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The npm package `dsh-kb-rag` is published from `npm-package/`. One-page overview: docs/promo.html. F"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"orks and similarly named repositories are not release sources; the canonical repository is Breeze136"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"ilarly named repositories are not release sources; the canonical repository is Breeze136/dsh-kb-rag."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Figure 1　Every answer line traces back to a passage in your library: section, page, DOI, and who tha"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"nswer line traces back to a passage in your library: section, page, DOI, and who that passage cites."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Figure 2　All of it runs on your machine: chunking, embedding, keyword plus vector search, then a loc"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ll of it runs on your machine: chunking, embedding, keyword plus vector search, then a local rerank."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## What a result looks like"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"A `kb_rag` call returns evidence in this shape. The interface is in Chinese today, so the block belo"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"w is a translation. `[in-library]` marks a cited work that is already indexed."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Authors, journals and DOIs are placeholders; the format is real. The full walkthrough is in `docs/OU"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"s and DOIs are placeholders; the format is real. The full walkthrough is in `docs/OUTPUT-FORMAT.md`."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Follow the citations"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"A passage keeps the citation marks printed in the PDF. kb-rag resolves each mark against the\nlibrary"},{"id":"p14s2","text":", so `[4, 7]` becomes two entries: one you already hold, with its own page number, and\none that is s"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"till outside — a lead to fetch rather than a dead end."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Figure 3　Solid arrows are citations the parser resolved; the line at the bottom is a related work, n"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" arrows are citations the parser resolved; the line at the bottom is a related work, not a citation."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Refilling is a loop"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Add an outside reference — by DOI with `kb_fetch`, or by dropping the PDF into the folder and\ningest"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ing again — and its own reference list enters the next search. The same question then\nreturns more e"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"vidence and a longer chain to follow. Indexing stays incremental: unchanged files\nare skipped, nothi"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"longer chain to follow. Indexing stays incremental: unchanged files\nare skipped, nothing is rebuilt."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Figure 4　Ref 7 was outside the library; after refilling it opens at p.9, and its own Ref 9 becomes t"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"7 was outside the library; after refilling it opens at p.9, and its own Ref 9 becomes the next lead."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## What 1.6.8 changes"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"1.6.8 fixes two things that broke the DSH 0.2 install: the peer range and the client injection list."},{"id":"p20s2","text":" With both wrong, the plugin was rejected during install and the tool cards stayed empty."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The release also adds HTML answer pages rendered by the engine and a title-level probe. `kb_stats` n"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ow reports model cache state, and deep searches return `no_hit` when the best reranked score stays b"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"elow the floor. The search core is otherwise unchanged: on the same library, results line up with 1."},{"id":"p21s4","text":"6.7. The full list is in CHANGELOG.md."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"kb-rag runs in the DSH desktop app. Install it from the plugin panel. The command-line routes exist "},{"id":"p23s2","text":"for maintainers and old web deployments; new users do not need them."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Engine capabilities"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- Chunking is section-aware: abstracts get weight 1.5, methods 1.2. It also handles inline headings,"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" abstract promotion, caption blocks and paragraph merging for non-article documents.\n- Retrieval com"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"bines BM25 (with CJK bigrams), bge-small vector cosine, RRF fusion and section weights.\n- Reranking "},{"id":"p25s4","text":"uses bge-reranker-base to cut the top 20 down to 3, with a bge-large-en bi-encoder as fallback.\n- Ev"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"ery passage carries its PDF page and section. The page renders as `section · p.N` and maps onto Zote"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"ro's `?page=N` link.\n- In-text `[n]` markers resolve to reference entries. Nature-style superscripts"},{"id":"p25s7","text":" are detected from font metrics, so `graphene1,2` becomes `graphene[1,2]`. Cited works are matched b"},{"id":"p25s8","text":"y DOI, normalised title, or first author plus year, and in-library matches are marked.\n- SHA-256 has"},{"id":"p25s9","text":"hes skip unchanged files (about 40× faster on re-runs) and catch duplicate copies across folders.\n- "},{"id":"p25s10","text":"Each document records the parser revision that wrote it (`docs.indexed_with`), so `kb_stats` can rep"},{"id":"p25s11","text":"ort rows an older revision left behind.\n- Identical queries hit a cache. Any ingest or engine rebuil"},{"id":"p25s12","text":"d clears it.\n- The engine runs as a resident daemon. Models load once, the daemon recovers from cras"},{"id":"p25s13","text":"hes, and it is released when the plugin stops.\n- If the library's vectors were built with a differen"},{"id":"p25s14","text":"t embedding model, retrieval stops with an explicit error instead of falling back to keyword search."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- Scanned PDFs are not supported. Documents without a text layer are skipped; OCR is out of scope.\n-"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" Page anchors are PDF-only. TXT, MD and DOCX files, and documents indexed before schema v3, fall bac"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"k to section-level location until re-ingested with `force`.\n- Citation linking requires a re-ingest."},{"id":"p29s4","text":" Superscript detection and reference splitting run at parse time.\n- Metadata is only as good as the "},{"id":"p29s5","text":"PDF. It is never 100% accurate; when it is missing, title and year are judged from the cover page, a"},{"id":"p29s6","text":"nd existing Zotero metadata is preferred.\n- Captions are searchable as text; content that exists onl"},{"id":"p29s7","text":"y inside a figure is not.\n- Keyword matching is in memory. Beyond a few hundred thousand chunks, FAI"},{"id":"p29s8","text":"SS HNSW or SQLite FTS5 would be the next step.\n- Some publishers redirect automated PDF requests to "},{"id":"p29s9","text":"a login page. `kb_fetch` reports the failure and leaves the manual path (download, then `kb_ingest`)"},{"id":"p29s10","text":"_fetch` reports the failure and leaves the manual path (download, then `kb_ingest`) as the fallback."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
